sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Fraud alert investigation and resolution
    accDescr: Illustrative fraud-alert case sequence covering alert enrichment, urgent containment, evidence rework, investigation, recovery, loss handling, and documented terminal outcomes.

    autonumber
    participant Detection as Detection Service
    participant Case as Case Service
    participant Analyst
    participant Operations as Product Operations
    participant Customer

    Detection->>Case: Create alert and preserve event evidence
    Case->>Case: Check alert data completeness
    alt Alert data is incomplete
        Case->>Detection: Request transaction, customer, or device enrichment
        Detection-->>Case: Supply available context
    else Alert data is complete
        Case->>Case: Record case readiness
    end
    Case->>Analyst: Assign risk-prioritized case
    Analyst->>Case: Assess potential impact and containment need

    alt Immediate containment is needed
        Case->>Operations: Apply proportionate hold or restriction
        Operations-->>Case: Confirm control applied
        Case->>Customer: Notify when appropriate
    else Immediate containment is not needed
        Case->>Case: Record no immediate restriction
    end

    loop Until evidence is sufficient or a controlled decision is made
        Analyst->>Case: Review activity, identity, and prior alerts
        alt Evidence is insufficient
            Analyst->>Customer: Request clarification or supporting information
            Customer-->>Analyst: Provide information, or indicate it is unavailable
            opt Information remains unavailable by the deadline
                Analyst->>Case: Escalate incomplete case for controlled decision
            end
        else Evidence is sufficient
            Analyst->>Case: Record investigation finding
        end
    end

    alt Fraud or misuse is not supported
        Analyst->>Case: Document rationale and alert-tuning feedback
        Note over Case,Analyst: Terminal outcome: close as no fraud identified
    else Fraud or misuse is supported
        Analyst->>Operations: Confirm affected products and funds
        alt Reversal or recovery is viable
            Operations->>Operations: Initiate recall, reversal, or recovery
            Operations-->>Case: Record recovered or unrecovered result
        else Recovery is not viable
            Operations-->>Case: Record loss and begin applicable claims handling
        end
        Case->>Customer: Communicate outcome and remediation
        Case->>Case: Record controls and monitoring actions
        Note over Case,Customer: Terminal outcome: close case and monitor recurrence
    end
